│ To resolve the issue with the literalinclude directive in Sphinx,  │
│ where the prepend and append directives are causing incorrect      │
│ indentation, we need to modify the logic that processes these      │
│ directives. The current implementation strips leading whitespace,  │
│ which is essential for maintaining the correct formatting of the   │
│ included content.                                                  │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                            ✅ Reasoning                            │
│                                                                    │
│ The literalinclude directive in Sphinx is processed by the         │
│ LiteralInclude class, which handles the prepend and append         │
│ directives. The current implementation strips the leading          │
│ whitespace when applying these directives, which causes the        │
│ indentation to be incorrect. To fix this, we need to ensure that   │
│ the prepend and append directives are applied without stripping    │
│ the original leading whitespace.                                   │
│                                                                    │
│ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │
│                              ✅ Patch                              │
│                                                                    │
│ [file]sphinx/ext/literalinclude.py[/file] [original] def           │
│ process_literalinclude(self, env, literalinclude): # Existing code │
│ that strips leading whitespace env.add_line('...') [/original]     │
│ [patched] def process_literalinclude(self, env, literalinclude): # │
│ Preserve leading whitespace when applying prepend/append # Extract │
│ the content to be included content =                               │
│ env.get_content(literalinclude)                                    │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
│  # Apply prepend and append directives                             │
│  if ':prepend:' in literalinclude:                                 │
│      content = self._apply_prepend(content, literalinclude)        │
│  if ':append:' in literalinclude:                                  │
│      content = self._apply_append(content, literalinclude)         │
│                                                                    │
│  # Add the content to the environment                              │
│  env.add_line(content)                                             │
│                                                                    │
│                                                                    │
